*14 Letters*

Robert and Peter had applied for jobs at a large company and had to take
an intelligence test.

Both of them found the test a breeze, except that they admitted to being
momentarily stumped by the final question: "Name a 14 letter word for
someone in charge of a plant."

"How did you answer that last one?" asked Robert.  "I thought it was
tough at first....  then I thought of *Superintendent*."

"I think I got it right too," Pete said.  "But I wrote down
Horticulturist."

